  "answer_core": "Do not choose your dissertation direction yet. Treat the next short window as a low‑cost test with two evidence gates.\n\nFirst gate: the Silva/data path. Speak with your advisor before involving anyone else. Then use a brief, time‑bounded check with Dr. Silva to verify concrete facts: what data exists, who controls access, when you can see it, what collaboration terms look like, and what portion of the work would clearly be yours. Only continue if these answers show a realistic, finishable dissertation path and your advisor explicitly supports the move.\n\nSecond gate: the fallback. Confirm it truly remains viable—your advisor keeps it resourced, you can re‑enter without penalty, and it can carry a full dissertation. Set a clear stop date and visible conditions for saying no to the Silva direction.\n\nRun only these two probes for the next couple of weeks. Do not develop a full proposal, do not attempt to advance all options in parallel, and do not extrapolate from broad PhD success statistics to this specific choice. Make the actual decision only once you have evidence on both gates.",
